<RequirementsAnalysis VERSION="0.2.0">
  <Project>
    <name>PaymentService</name>
    <solution-file>PaymentServices.sln</solution-file>
    <annotation>High-throughput SWIFT-like payment processing microservice in MIF (Micro Integrator for Finances). Built on .NET 9 CQRS + Dapr + Wolverine Sagas. Reader API for query path, Writer API for command path, Worker processes sagas via MQ, all persisted to MongoDB. Deployed on Kubernetes with horizontal scaling.</annotation>
    <keywords>mif, payment-processing, swift, cqrs, dapr, wolverine, mongodb, k8s, horizontal-scaling, saga, message-partitioning, serilog, xunit</keywords>
  </Project>

  <Actors>
    <actor-SenderBank>External banking system initiating a payment instruction (SWIFT-like message).</actor-SenderBank>
    <actor-ReceiverBank>External banking system receiving the final settlement notification.</actor-ReceiverBank>
    <actor-Operator>Platform operations engineer monitoring throughput, latency, and error budgets.</actor-Operator>
    <actor-System>Internal automated actors — Reader (read queries), Writer (command gateway), Worker (saga processor on MQ).</actor-System>
  </Actors>

  <UseCases>
    <UC-001>
      <Actor>SenderBank</Actor>
      <Action>Sends a payment instruction via Writer API (command path)</Action>
      <Goal>The payment is validated, routed to Worker via MQ, processed through a saga, and settled with ReceiverBank</Goal>
      <Preconditions>Writer API is live; MQ is configured; Worker instances are subscribed to payment saga topic</Preconditions>
      <AcceptanceCriteria>End-to-end latency ≤ 2s p99; zero message loss; saga completion emits settlement confirmation</AcceptanceCriteria>
      <Priority>critical</Priority>
      <RelatedFlows>DF-PAYMENT-LIFECYCLE</RelatedFlows>
    </UC-001>

    <UC-002>
      <Actor>Operator</Actor>
      <Action>Queries payment status via Reader API (query path)</Action>
      <Goal>Retrieve the current saga state and all intermediate steps for a given payment from MongoDB</Goal>
      <Preconditions>Correlation ID is known; MongoDB read replica is available</Preconditions>
      <AcceptanceCriteria>Response includes full timeline: received → validated → processed → settled; query latency ≤ 100ms p95</AcceptanceCriteria>
      <Priority>high</Priority>
      <RelatedFlows>DF-PAYMENT-QUERY</RelatedFlows>
    </UC-002>

    <UC-003>
      <Actor>System</Actor>
      <Action>Reader ingests payment queries at high concurrency (thousands/sec) from the read-only query path</Action>
      <Goal>Queries are served from MongoDB without blocking write-path processing</Goal>
      <Preconditions>MongoDB read-only connection pool is configured; Reader API instances are scaled per load</Preconditions>
      <AcceptanceCriteria>Read p99 latency ≤ 100ms; no impact on write-path (Writer→MQ→Worker)</AcceptanceCriteria>
      <Priority>high</Priority>
      <RelatedFlows>DF-PAYMENT-QUERY</RelatedFlows>
    </UC-004>

    <UC-004>
      <Actor>System</Actor>
      <Action>Writer API routes payment commands to Worker via MQ with partition key (correlationId)</Action>
      <Goal>Messages are partitioned by MQ broker and routed to the correct Worker instance without cross-shard contention</Goal>
      <Preconditions>Dapr pub/sub component configured with partition key; Worker instances scaled per partition count</Preconditions>
      <AcceptanceCriteria>No single partition hot-spots under 1000 msg/s per partition; backpressure triggers scaling events</AcceptanceCriteria>
      <Priority>critical</Priority>
      <RelatedFlows>DF-COMMAND-PARTITION</RelatedFlows>
    </UC-005>

    <UC-005>
      <Actor>System</Actor>
      <Action>Worker saga handles payment lifecycle: validation → enrichment → settlement → notification</Action>
      <Goal>Saga compensates on failure; idempotency ensures no double-settlement</Goal>
      <Preconditions>Idempotency key derived from message; MongoDB supports transactional saga state updates</Preconditions>
      <AcceptanceCriteria>Saga compensation runs within 5s of failure detection; no duplicate settlements observed</AcceptanceCriteria>
      <Priority>critical</Priority>
      <RelatedFlows>DF-SAGA-LIFECYCLE</RelatedFlows>
    </UC-006>
    <UC-007>
      <Actor>AccountHolder</Actor>
      <Action>Queries transaction history for an account via Reader API</Action>
      <Goal>Retrieve paged list of payments where the account appears as sender or receiver, sorted by date descending</Goal>
      <Preconditions>Account ID is known; MongoDB index on sender/receiver exists</Preconditions>
      <AcceptanceCriteria>Response includes full payment timeline for each transaction; query latency ≤ 200ms p95</AcceptanceCriteria>
      <Priority>high</Priority>
      <RelatedFlows>DF-STATEMENT-QUERY</RelatedFlows>
    </UC-007>
  </UseCases>

  <NonGoals>
    <item-1>No real-time FX conversion in v1 — settlement is single-currency only.</item-1>
    <item-2>No web UI or admin dashboard — operator access is CLI/API only.</item-2>
    <item-3>No direct SWIFT network integration in v1 — accepts SWIFT-like structured messages via HTTP.</item-3>
    <item-4>No multi-tenancy beyond the single service boundary; identity/auth delegated to IdentityService.</item-4>
  </NonGoals>

  <Constraints>
    <constraint-1>Must achieve ≥ 1000 payment messages/second sustained throughput under 3-replica Writer + 3-replica Worker.</constraint-1>
    <constraint-2>Must not lose in-flight messages during rolling deployment or pod eviction (at-least-once delivery).</constraint-2>
    <constraint-3>All structured logs must include correlationId; secrets and PII (account numbers, amounts) must be redacted at the Serilog enricher level.</constraint-3>
    <constraint-4>Dapr sidecar must be present in every pod (Reader, Writer, Worker) for pub/sub and state management.</constraint-4>
    <constraint-5>MongoDB must be configured with replica-set for transactional saga state persistence.</constraint-5>
    <constraint-6>Read path (Reader API) must not interfere with write path (Writer→MQ→Worker). Separate connection pools.</constraint-6>
  </Constraints>

  <Risks>
    <risk-1>Message ordering within a partition: if Wolverine sagas depend on strict ordering per correlationId, partition key design is critical.</risk-1>
    <risk-2>Idempotency gaps: if the same payment message is replayed by the MQ after partial saga progress, duplicate steps must be detected and skipped.</risk-2>
    <risk-3>Dapr pub/sub component latency at scale: verify that the Dapr pub/sub component sustains the required throughput under partition fan-out.</risk-3>
    <risk-4>Cold-start saga hydration from MongoDB: large saga state documents may add latency when the Worker restarts and replays pending sagas.</risk-4>
    <risk-5>Read-write consistency: MongoDB eventual consistency window may show stale payment states on Reader queries immediately after saga completion.</risk-5>
  </Risks>

  <OpenQuestions>
    <question-1>Dapr pub/sub component config: which transport? Kafka is preferred for partition-native scaling.</question-1>
    <question-2>SWIFT message format: ISO 20022 (XML) or MT (tag-based)? Affects message schema and validation.</question-2>
    <question-3>How does Writer API authenticate requests? mTLS, API key, or Keycloak tokens from IdentityService?</question-3>
    <question-4>Idempotency key derivation: hash(paymentId + amount + timestamp) or business-level key?</question-4>
  </OpenQuestions>
</RequirementsAnalysis>
